  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of integrated multisectoral humanitarian assistance to vulnerable populations in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan continues to face a critical humanitarian crisis, with 9.3 million people in need due to conflict, displacement, and climate shocks, including severe flooding. Economic instability, inadequate services, and an influx of returnees from Sudan have worsened vulnerabilities, driving urgent water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH), protection, and shelter needs across the country.This Action contributes to addressing protection risks while alleviating the humanitarian needs of vulnerable groups, including internally displaced persons (IDPs), returnees from Sudan, and host communities. IOM is providing lifesaving multi-sectoral assistance in a safe, dignified, and inclusive manner. IOM&#x2019;s intervention focuses on WASH, shelter and non-food items (S-NFI), camp coordination and camp management (CCCM), protection, and cash services tailored to the needs of the affected populations. To strengthen the response, IOM continues to provide evidence-based data by enhancing information management through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) and, as part of its Core Pipeline role, procure and preposition WASH and S-NFI kits for the most affected communities. Considering the ongoing Sudan conflict and the continued influx of returnees, IOM will continue to provide onward transportation assistance (OTA) for returnees stranded at border points and deliver emergency aid at transit centres.</narrative>
  </description>
